         redistribution with notices are permitted; selling the rules is not.

Vendored subtrees: the security/ and correctness/ rule directories of go/ and
python/. Only rule YAML is copied; the per-rule test fixtures (*.go, *.py, ...
and *.test.yaml) are left behind. Rules listed in sync.sh's DROPPED table are
then removed, each with a recorded reason (another gate owns the finding class,
or the rule is a false positive for this codebase).

Regenerate with: .semgrep/sync.sh [<commit-sha>]

Why not semgrep/semgrep-rules: that set ships under the "Semgrep Rules License
v1.0" — internal business use only, no offering the rules "as a service", and
copies must keep the notices. opengrep-rules (LGPL 2.1 + Commons Clause) permits
internal use and redistribution with notices, which fits vendoring here.
